><surname>Lycett</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Mahairaki</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Siden-Kiamos</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Louis</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Laminin and the malaria parasite's journey through the mosquito midgut.</article-title><source>J Exp Biol</source><volume>208</volume><fpage>2497</fpage><lpage>2502</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15961736</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003672-Frolet1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frolet</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Thoma</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Blandin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoffmann</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Levashina</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Boosting NF-kappaB-dependent basal immunity of Anopheles gambiae aborts development of Plasmodium berghei.</article-title><source>Immunity</source><volume>25</volume><fpage>677</fpage><lpage>685</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17045818</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003672-Michel1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Michel</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Budd</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Pinto</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gibson</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kafatos</surname><given-names>FC</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Anopheles gambiae SRPN2 facilitates midgut invasion by the malaria parasite Plasmodium berghei.</article-title><source>EMBO Rep</source><volume>6</volume><fpage>891</fpage><lpage>897<